    description: "STATEMENT. Work a test keeps for later tests is paired with every test that is handed it, including work kept by a closure that a module-, class- or session-scoped fixture hands out.\n\nVIOLATED (campaign 3 of WI-gojov, 2026-11-18). packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_axiom_falsification.py: the module-scoped fixture `survey` returns `run(name, files)`, which keeps each fixture repo's behavior map in a dict it closes over. run_behavior_map runs inside the FIRST test that asks for a name; every later test with that name is handed the map and has no row for the analysis. Two planted faults (framework_patterns._read_framework_patterns 'assign None'; taxonomy.get_language 'negate if') failed 12 tests of this file that the by-statement selector would leave out; each fails alone with the fault and passes alone without it. test_visibility_follows_the_languages_rule[go-unexported] has 27 recorded blocks, none in taxonomy.py or framework_patterns.py.\n\nWHY THE GUARD MISSED IT. kept_work_guard scans module state writes and lazy attributes; a container captured by a closure of a broader-scope fixture is neither. An AST scan of every test file finds one fixture of this shape (this one).\n\nFIX. (1) `run` marks itself: kept_work.used(run, name) on every call, `with kept_work.filling(run, name):` around the survey. (2) kept_work_guard reports a closure of a fixture whose scope is not 'function' that writes a container or name of its enclosing function (subscript store, append/add/update/setdefault/extend, nonlocal) and is not marked, as an unmarked state write.\n\nCLOSE CONDITION. After a recording full run, select_by_statement on each of the two faults keeps all 12 tests (command and output in the notebook); the guard fails on the unmarked fixture (test) and passes the live tree; merged.\n\nEVIDENCE. ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/bar/campaign3_summary.txt, campaign3/replay/."  # 0a09
    fields:  # 0a09
      statement: "Work a test keeps for later tests (including a closure that a module-, class- or session-scoped fixture hands out) is paired with every test that is handed it."  # 0a09
      root_cause: "The module-scoped fixture survey in test_axiom_falsification.py hands out a closure that keeps behavior maps in a dict it closes over; the recorder sees no boundary, and kept_work_guard scans only module state and lazy attributes."  # 0a09
